WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.350
Rick and Morty season 5 is coming and it's
sure to be full of all the little details

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.970
and subtle jokes that we've come to expect.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.190
Here are a few we saw in the new trailer.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.920
In the trailer, there's a strange-looking
character with slicked-back hair, pale blue

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.150
lips, gills on his neck, and very little clothing.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.520
This guy is actually someone Rick detests
more than any other creature in any other

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.390
universe, and the Rick and Morty season 5
trailer isn't the first time fans have caught

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.520
a glimpse of him.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.469
Back in July 2020, Adult Swim released a first-look
clip from the upcoming season, which features

00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:37.250
incomplete animation of Rick and Morty escaping
monsters on a ravaged planet, Morty driving

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:42.590
Rick's ship and dodging flaming asteroids,
and then crashing the ship in the ocean.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:47.690
Rick immediately panics, and then, the merman
emerges from a giant clamshell to taunt Rick

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:48.690
and Morty.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.320
His name is Mr. Nimbus, and he's Rick's "once
and eternal foe."

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.360
"Who the [bleep] is that?"

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.360
"My nemesis."

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.360
"What?"

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.750
"My [bleep]ing nemesis, okay?"

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:58.750
"

00:00:58.750 --> 00:00:59.750
Okay, but what was his name again?"

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.240
"I am Mr. Nimbus!"

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.680
Another short sequence in the season 5 trailer
depicts Morty carrying an injured Rick through

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.740
a landscape dotted with floating crystals
that look like a good place to store renegade

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.280
Kryptonian generals.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.250
In Rick and Morty, however, these crystals
aren't gateways to the Phantom Zone; rather,

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.720
they seem to reveal alternate universe versions
of Rick and Morty.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.850
And it wouldn't be the show we all know and
love if at least one of these alternate realities

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.170
didn't show Rick and Morty as superheroes.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.920
As the pair trek through the field of crystals,
Rick is quick to point out the crystal that

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.979
shows the reality in which they are both versions
of the half-vampiric, vampire-killing Marvel

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:38.550
hero Blade, famously played on screen by Wesley
Snipes.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.810
This seems to be a clever reference to the
bloody rave scene from Blade.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:47.270
The Blade-universe crystal is only on screen
for a few seconds in the Rick and Morty season

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:50.880
5 trailer, but it isn't the only one that
bears weight.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.600
Way in the back of the same shot is another
significant crystal — one that references

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.340
Rick and Morty's origins.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.310
In the crystal, Morty's wearing a blue shirt
and a red vest, while Rick still rocks his

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.150
signature white lab coat.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:08.390
If, upon closer inspection, this looks familiar
to fans, it's because they've almost definitely

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:11.529
seen these exact iterations of Rick and Morty
before.

00:02:11.529 --> 00:02:15.879
This crystal's reality is a callback to "The
Real Animated Adventures of Doc and Mharti

00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:20.379
," made by Rick and Morty co-creator Justin
Roiland in 2006.

00:02:20.379 --> 00:02:25.959
This very-NSFW short parodies the classic
Back to the Future film series, and ultimately

00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:28.239
formed the basis for Rick and Morty.

00:02:28.239 --> 00:02:32.309
"Guess you guys aren't ready for that yet.

00:02:32.309 --> 00:02:34.530
But your kids are going to love it."

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:39.489
Part of the fun of Rick and Morty is all the
clever satire of popular sci-fi and fantasy

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:44.560
properties, and season 5 looks to continue
this tradition by taking aim at two IPs in

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.560
particular.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:50.060
A common sight in the trailer is the Smith-Sanchez
family geared up in a set of matching, color-coded

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.060
suits.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.310
This feels like a clear reference to the classic
'80s cartoon Voltron.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:59.309
The trailer also seems to give a hat-tip to
another popular kids TV series: Transformers.

00:02:59.309 --> 00:03:03.959
Early on in the Rick and Morty season 5 trailer,
we see Rick's ship facing off against a humanoid

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:08.930
robot that bears a striking resemblance to
a Transformer, with car parts making up certain

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:10.549
portions of its body.

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:15.519
At several points in the trailer, Rick and
Beth are seen wearing some gruesome costumes

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:17.650
that look straight out of a horror movie.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:21.680
Fittingly, they are from a horror movie — or
rather, a horror franchise.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.000
These outfits prove that the series will reference
the late '80s horror film Hellraiser in at

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.900
least one upcoming episode.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.680
The whole universe in which Rick and Beth
wear these costumes appears to be a parody

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:36.700
of the Hellraiser world, and the get-ups look
like mildly toned-down versions of what the

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.650
film's extra-dimensional Cenobite beings wear.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:44.059
The darts in Beth's face feel like a clever
twist on the iron nails that the film's main

00:03:44.059 --> 00:03:46.809
antagonist, Pinhead, has all over his face.

00:03:46.809 --> 00:03:50.629
Additionally, in the background of one scene
from the trailer are two creatures who appear

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:53.769
to be riffs on Hellraiser's creepier Cenobites.

00:03:53.769 --> 00:03:58.889
In particular, the one with no eyes and who
bears all of its teeth looks exactly like

00:03:58.889 --> 00:04:01.250
Chatterer, Hellraiser's right-hand man.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:05.299
The one between Rick and Beth, with half of
its face splayed open, could be a very subtle

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:09.690
reference to Angelique from Hellraiser: Bloodline,
though it's more likely that this one is a

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:10.919
Rick and Morty original.

00:04:11.919 --> 00:04:16.690
The thought of his longtime crush Jessica
being a significant part of his life is enough

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.780
to make Morty scream until he passes out.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.420
That thought will apparently become a reality
in Rick and Morty season 5, as the trailer

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:28.870
shows two separate instances in which Jessica
appears as part of Smith-Sanchez family adventures.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.760
Though she has been seen in missions with
the crew before, some were non-canonical and

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.650
these season 5 moments hold much more weight.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:40.540
Early in the trailer, there's a scene involving
giant, Transformers-esque robots.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:44.980
Upon first glance, it looks like Rick, Morty,
and Summer are in the battle arena, but it's

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:47.690
actually Rick, Morty, and Jessica.

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:50.980
Why would Jessica be involved in such a strange
quest?

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:56.010
The answer lies in the first-look clip from
season 5, the same one that revealed Mr. Nimbus.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:05:00.000
In that clip, Morty calls Jessica and confesses
his affection for her.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.570
Much to Morty's surprise, Jessica admits she
has feelings for Morty too, and invites him

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.560
to watch a movie with her that night.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.000
Though it's not explained in the new trailer,
that moment should happen in season 5 and

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.150
mark the beginning of a relationship between
Jessica and Morty.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:18.511
Of course, the most important detail in the
whole trailer comes right at the end: New

00:05:18.511 --> 00:05:23.660
episodes of Rick and Morty will be portaling
into this universe on Adult Swim on Sunday,

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:27.380
June 20 at 11 PM ET.

